\name{ComplexHeatmapTreeLayerProcessor}
\alias{ComplexHeatmapTreeLayerProcessor}
\title{ComplexHeatmap Dendrogram Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads the dendrograms a ComplexHeatmap heat map draws on one side, rows
or columns, as \code{tree} layers, from the \code{HeatmapList} its drawing returned
(\code{\link[=complexheatmap_capture]{complexheatmap_capture()}}); see \code{\link[=complexheatmap_trees]{complexheatmap_trees()}} for which are
read and \code{\link[=complexheatmap_tree_nodes]{complexheatmap_tree_nodes()}} for the nodes. Experimental.

Each leaf is named as the heat layer names its row or column
(\link{ComplexHeatmapLayerProcessor}), in the same order.

\strong{Selectors.} None. 'ComplexHeatmap' draws a dendrogram as segments,
several to a merge and nothing at a leaf, with no element per node; a
highlight that cannot be aligned with a node is left out rather than
placed on the wrong link.
}
